1. e4 c5 2. f4 Nc6 3. Nf3 g6 4. Bb5 Bg7 5. Bxc6 dxc6 6. d3 Nf6 7. Nc3 O-O 8. O-O b6 {Conditions are perfect for a kingside attack: Black has little counterplay as White's central pawn chain is so secure.} 9. Qe1! Ne8 10. Qh4 (10. f5! {It is stronger to play this immediately - see the next note.}) 10... Nd6 ({It is quite an ugly move, but I think Black's only chance of stemming the attack is to play} 10... f5!? {, blocking White's f-pawn and so hemming in the bishop on c1.}) 11. f5 {[%cal Rf4f5,Rc1h6] The standard sacrifice, and under even better conditions than normal: manoeuvering the knight to d6 has not helped Black in any way.} gxf5 12. e5 Ne8 13. Bh6 (13. Ng5? Qd4+ {wouldn't be clever.}) 13... f6 14. Kh1 Bxh6 15. Qxh6 Ng7 16. Rae1 Be6 17. Ne2 c4 18. Nf4 cxd3 19. cxd3 Bxa2 (19... Qd7 20. Re3 {followed by a swing to g3 or h3.}) 20. e6 Qc8 21. Re3 Nxe6 22. Nxe6 Bxe6 23. Rxe6 Rf7 (23... Qxe6 24. Ng5 {. Neat.}) 24. Rfe1 Qd7 25. Nh4 Re8 26. Nxf5 Qxd3 27. Nd6 1-0

